    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0393" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/821: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macedo Soares</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-20">February 20, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received 6:40
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to communicate to Your Excellency that the President of the
                    Republic of the United States of Brazil confers, by <pb facs="0394" n="295"
                        xml:id="pg295"/> the present telegram, full powers on the Ambassador of
                    Brazil at your capital, Mr. Oswaldo Aranha, to sign, as representative of the
                    Brazilian Government and of the Bank of Brazil (<hi rendition="#italic">Banco do
                        Brasil</hi>), with the National Foreign Trade Council an agreement for the
                    liquidation of the commercial debts between Brazil and the United States of
                    America which are overdue.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José Carlos de Macedo
                        Soares</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
